We're a little over a month away from the launch of <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, and Apple is continuing to make changes. The fifth beta of &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; changes the look of some app icons and adjusts Liquid Glass, plus it adds some smaller features that make the iPhone just a little nicer to use.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/iOS-27-Feature-Cool.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1056261" /><br/>
<h2>App Icons</h2><br/>
There are updated Liquid Glass icons for Safari, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a>, Settings, Remote, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a>, and Preview. Some of the icons have been entirely redesigned, while others feature more detail than before.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-b5-icons.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059151" /><br/>
<h2>Siri AI Voice Customization</h2><br/>
Voice customizations for &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI have been expanded, and Pace and Expressivity can be adjusted for all seven American voices and the four British voices.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-siri-voice.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059148" /><br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI voice customization is done on-device, so the feature is limited the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17-pro/">iPhone 17 Pro</a>, &zwnj;iPhone 17 Pro&zwnj; Max, or <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a>.<br/>
<h2>Contacts</h2><br/>
If a contact you've created has a company associated with it, the company name will show in the contact list under the name and in search. It makes it easier to see more information on a contact without having to tap into the contact card.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-contacts-company-name.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059165" /><br/>
<h2>Create a Pass</h2><br/>
The Apple Wallet Create a Pass feature is now available outside of the U.S.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/ios-27-wallet-create-pass.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1051256" /><br/>
<h2>Splash Screens</h2><br/>
Apple added splash screens for the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a>, Wallet, and Music apps, explaining what's new in &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-beta-5-splash-screens.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059159" /><br/>
<h2>Search and Ask</h2><br/>
Apple made minor changes to the animation when bringing up Search or Ask. The suggestions interface now comes up as the search bar does rather than popping up slightly afterward.<br/>
<br/>
The search interface also now has a "Search the Web" option at the bottom of results that was not there before.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Apps in Search</h2><br/>
You can now decide whether search should show app results, and if so, how many. You can turn off app results, have it show four apps, or have it show eight apps. There's also a toggle for showing app shortcuts.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-search-show-apps.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059160" /><br/>
<h2>Control Center</h2><br/>
When connected to Wi-Fi, the Control Center no longer shows information on cellular connection.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/07/ios-27-control-center-5g.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1055341" /><em>The &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; Control Center in beta 4</em></div><br/>
<h2>5G</h2><br/>
5G+ is now <a href="https://x.com/ifrnb/status/2086880920703803528?s=20">available in Spain</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Software Updates</h2><br/>
When you look at your software version in Settings > General > About, it now tells you when the last update was installed.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-beta-5-installed-today.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059161" /><br/>
<br/>
<h2>Clock</h2><br/>
There is a thicker font for the Alarms and Timers section of the Clock app.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-beta-5-alarm-font.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059164" /><br/>
<h2>Liquid Glass</h2><br/>
The clearest Liquid Glass setting is clearer than it was in the prior beta.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-beta-5-translucency.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059163" /><br/>
<h2>Mail</h2><br/>
There's now a toggle for the Personalize Smart Replies feature in the Mail app. It's off by default and can be turned on in the Mail section of the Settings app. <br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/08/ios-27-beta-5-mail-personalize-replies.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1059162" /><br/>
<h2>Battery</h2><br/>
